        "deep_dive": "### Mechanism of the Week: The Hallmarks of Aging\nThe hallmarks of aging are a set of twelve biological processes whose age-associated changes meet three criteria: they appear with advancing age, their experimental accentuation speeds aging, and their therapeutic targeting can slow, stop, or reverse aspects of aging in model systems. The original nine hallmarks were proposed in 2013 and later expanded to twelve to include disabled macroautophagy, chronic inflammation, and dysbiosis. Each hallmar",
        "trials": "### Trial Tracker\n- TAME (Targeting Aging with Metformin): metformin, Phase 3 planning stage; next milestone not dated in sources.\n- Viking obesity maintenance trial: unnamed obesity drug, late-stage; weight maintenance data reported.\n- Beacon XLRP trial: laru-zova gene therapy, Phase 3; primary endpoint met.\n- Huntington’s intermittent fasting pilot: intermittent fasting, pilot randomized; improvements observed, larger trials requested.\n\nThis episode marks the debut of Longevity Weekly."
      },
